While observing a game at Croesus' castle I thought about whether it
might be a good idea to have the possibility to use wands of locking
or spells of wizard lock to "lock"/disable bear traps and land mines
in line of fire. Currently the two locking features do not have many
applications and the new additional feature would not be unbalancing.
Zapping locking to disable falling rock traps wouldn't be bad either.

Some spoiler below!

Even the interesting application of using locking to lock trapdoors
would have more practical uses if possible to apply that in line of
fire[*] instead of being functional only if zapped down (as it is
currently implemented).

[*] Which may be restricted to lock just the first trap so that you
won't close the row of trapdoors in the castle with a single zap.

